  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet, because the premise doesn't hold: `channel` is still read downstream.\n\n- **`analytics-ingest` requires it.** `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` reads `channel` from `OrderPlaced` with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. Its README (lines 27 and 31) and tests (`analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts:88` and `:158`) say a missing or unknown `channel` makes ingestion reject the whole event. It also writes `channel` to the `orders` table (`src/ingest.ts:17`). If orders-service stops sending it, every `OrderPlaced` event would be rejected with a `ContractViolationError`, and analytics would stop receiving orders.\n- **`billing-service` has a smaller dependency.** Its test helpers include `channel` in the sample event. I only saw tests, so I don't know whether its production code reads the field.\n\nThat repo belongs to another team and is read-only for me, so I can't fix it from here.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n\n1. **Remove `channel` from the order model only.** That means the `Order` and `NewOrder` types, validation, request parsing and the tests. The event would still need to carry `channel`, so I'd have to give it a placeholder or keep it from somewhere else. That's awkward, so I don't recommend it.\n2. **Remove it everywhere, as you asked.** This only makes sense once analytics-ingest (and billing, if needed) have stopped requiring it. I can do the orders-service side now, but it shouldn't be deployed before they change.\n3. **Do it in stages.** First analytics-ingest makes `channel` optional, then we remove it here. I can draft a note for that team.\n\nWhich would you like? I'd pick option 3 or option 2, depending on whether the analytics team has already agreed to the change.",
